{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/8448-hh-h-tr-point-allocations-among-hunters","id":8448,"title":"[HH/H:tR] Point Allocations Among Hunters","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2013-11-11T16:21:31-08:00","id":8448,"title":"[HH/H:tR] Point Allocations Among Hunters","content":"In the olden days, mere mortals got 6/4/3 for Attributes and 11/7/4 for Abilities. This was true of the original Hunter's Hunted, Year of the Hunter and Year of the Ally material, and even for Hunter: the Reckoning's Imbued. Two exceptions existed in Demon Hunter X, with Shr getting way, way more points and Strike Force 0 team members getting about the same as many monsters, but the lower values were used even for Kinfolk chargen.<br /> <br /> So, after remaining this way for years, we get Hunter's Hunted II, which uses a more generous allotment on par with the monsters (7/5/3, 13/9/5). Raising an odd question about whether or not that might also apply to the Imbued when the time comes to update. Fragility and less capability are mainstays of Reckoning, but they technically come from the same background as the HHII characters. Is there something to do, or am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T00:56:10-08:00","id":8663,"title":"","content":"Technically, HHII keeps the 6/4/3 spread and leaves the 7/5/3 as an option. Which HtR had in optional rules as well.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think it's that big of a deal as is. A larger Ability dole of starting dots means you don't have to toss most of your freebies at Abilities just to cover all the little essentials. It's only five dots after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T07:21:08-08:00","id":8786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/8448-hh-h-tr-point-allocations-among-hunters?p=8663#post8663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Technically, HHII keeps the 6/4/3 spread and leaves the 7/5/3 as an option. Which HtR had in optional rules as well.<br /> <br /> Personally, I don't think it's that big of a deal as is. A larger Ability dole of starting dots means you don't have to toss most of your freebies at Abilities just to cover all the little essentials. It's only five dots after all.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think part of my recollection of HH2 got wrapped around the SF0 chargen. Mind, I wasn't throwing a panic about humans getting more points than they used to. Just idly wondering if the Imbued would also be ending up with the same boost.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2013-11-12T09:49:20-08:00","id":8887,"title":"","content":"The Demon Hunter X book certainly had the most generous &quot;mortal&quot; hunter spreads. But they also had pretty restrictive builds (Shih had to spend 9 of their Freebies and half of their background dots on set allocations).<br /> <br /> I figure when it comes time for a *20th era HtR game (hopefully not in 6 years!) they'll either stick with the HtR base spread or move to the HHII one. But it is pretty hard to tell this far out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}